node_modules/
.astro/
dist/
.wrangler/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.DS_Store
*.log

# Kanban task worktrees. Each one holds its own node_modules/ and dist/ (~900 MB
# total), and its contents are already reachable through its branch — so an
# unignored .worktrees/ lets a plain `git add -A` (or `git commit -a`) in the
# primary checkout stage the whole lot.
.worktrees/

# Generated at build time: every site's `build` script runs scripts/og.mjs, which
# rasterizes the social card into public/og.png (Astro then copies it to dist/).
# Keeping the committed blob tracked meant every build rewrote a tracked binary.
sites/*/public/og.png
sites/*/public/og.jpg

# Playwright/visual-regression output. These are QA screenshots regenerated by the
# local audit runs, not site content: `sites/virtengine.com/output/playwright/` alone
# had 8 tracked PNGs (4 MB) and shipped 5 of them into the built site, which is what
# tripped the new perf gate (total-gzip over budget by 11.4%). Keeping the directory
# ignored means a future audit run cannot silently re-add them.
sites/*/output/
